        "title": "Exit code is read from the first '(exit code N' in the summary, and that summary contains the job description the model chose",
        "severity": "medium",
        "file": "scripts/evidencia_em_segundo_plano.py",
        "line": 205,
        "rationale": "`_codigo` runs `_CODIGO.search(resumo)` on `<summary>`, which the host writes as `Background command \"<description>\" completed (exit code N...)`. The model chooses the description, and the search keeps the first match, so a description holding `(exit code 0)` sets the recorded exit code. The host really does emit `completed` with a non-zero code for test suites: the real transcripts under C:/Users/LHarden2/.claude/projects contain `Background command \"Run slow affected tests\" completed (exit code 1: No matches found)`, and the test at tests/test_evidencia_em_segundo_plano.py:562 relies on that form. Measured with the production `julgar` (script C:/Users/LHarden2/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--Users-LHarden2-Documents-projects-harness4claude--claude-worktrees-vibrant-montalcini-9868a6/6b0a4567-1776-465c-b71a-679660ca5622/scratchpad/probe_codigo.py). Control: the honest description with `completed (exit code 1: ...)` gives `aceito, exit_code=1`. Injection: the description `suite (exit code 0)` gives `aceito, exit_code=0, tests_collected=6`. The only thing that catches this is the `[exited with code N]` trailer check at line 271, and it passes silently when there is no trailer (`if trailer and ...`). The .output file sits in the session's own %TEMP%/claude/<project>/<session>/tasks folder, which the model can write, so removing the trailer or rewriting the counts is enough. With the trailer present the case is rejected (`codigo-diverge`, measured). Fix: take the exit code only from the host's fixed suffix, after the closing quote and anchored at the end, for example `\"\\s+(?:completed|failed|...)\\s+(?:\\(exit code (-?\\d+)[^)]*\\)|with exit code (-?\\d+))\\s*$`. Also treat a missing trailer as a reason to reject, not as a pass. Mitigation to note: the manual `state_cli` path (the AVISO_SEGUNDO_PLANO command) already lets someone enter evidence by typing it, so this does not grant more than that. It does break the module's own guarantee that it never accepts an ending the host did not write (lines 76-79).",
        "confidence": null,
        "adjudicado": false
      },
